course: dictionary
lesson: 3821
title: Understanding forgiveness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forgiveness is a noun. It means you stop being angry with someone who hurt you, and you do not try to pay them back. The words around it give clues: «Forgiveness can take time; it is honest to say "I'm still upset, but I'm trying".» So forgiveness is often a slow process, not something that happens in one second.
explain: Look at «Above all, forgiveness is stronger than revenge.» Revenge means paying someone back for a hurt. Forgiveness is set against revenge, so it must be the opposite: letting go of the anger instead of hitting back.
explain: Forgiveness does not mean the wrong did not matter. In ethics lessons, pupils talk about whether you can forgive without forgetting. You can forgive someone and still remember what they did.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. Does «Many people say forgiveness is a gift you give yourself» still make sense if forgiveness means stopping being angry and not paying back? Yes, it does, so your meaning fits.
fact: Forgiveness is a noun.
fact: «Forgiveness» means stopping being angry with someone and not paying them back.
fact: Asking for forgiveness means saying sorry and hoping the other person will forgive you.
fact: In church, Christians pray for forgiveness, and the Lord's Prayer says "forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us".
fact: Forgiving someone does not mean the wrong did not matter.
exercise: «Many people say forgiveness is a gift you give yourself.» What does forgiveness mean in this sentence? | *Stopping being angry with someone and not paying them back | Buying something for a friend | Winning an argument | Forgetting your homework
exercise: «Forgiveness can take time; it is honest to say "I'm still upset, but I'm trying".» What does this sentence show? | Forgiveness is only for adults | Forgiveness means you forget everything | Forgiveness always happens in one second | *Forgiveness can be a slow process
exercise: Does forgiving someone mean the wrong did not matter? | Yes, but only if you are in church | *No, the wrong still matters | Yes, it means the wrong did not matter at all
test: «Ask for forgiveness» means | Forget what happened | *Say sorry and hope to be forgiven | Pay the other person back | Keep the anger going
test: In church, «forgiveness of sins» means | A payment for a wrong that was done | *Christians believe God offers forgiveness to people who are truly sorry | A church that is closed | A promise never to pray again
exam: «Above all, forgiveness is stronger than revenge» tells us that | Forgiveness is a kind of game | Revenge is always the better choice | *Forgiveness can be more powerful than paying someone back | Forgiveness is a weak, silly idea
